[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. The reports in it say
otherwise. Merging on subject ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) put
three problems with three different fixes into one ticket.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## The three problems

- **`parser`** ([ticket #1](https://github.com/mateuszl/what-it-shows/issues/1)): the shared
  parser reads every date month first, and every tenant here writes the day first. The reports
  show day and month swapped: "Booked for 7 June. The invite says 6 July."
- **`hint`** ([ticket #2](https://github.com/mateuszl/what-it-shows/issues/2)): booking-v3 prints
  `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. Day-first tenants' people type what it says, and the form
  reads it day first. Only form reports from booking-v3 tenants. Fixing the parser does not fix this.
- **one-day move** ([ticket #3](https://github.com/mateuszl/what-it-shows/issues/3)): the date
  moves by one day, not a month, and depends on where the reader is: "Client in Lisbon got
  Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday." These are the reports the table above footnotes as
  read as a one-day move. They stay counted under `parser`, where they're filed, and get a ticket
  of their own because a parser fix will not close them.

<Callout kind="warn">
Count by cause, not by subject or intake tag. Twelve subjects cover the same three problems,
and intake's tag disagrees with the cause on dozens of reports.
</Callout>

## How this page counts

The table is the desk's own cause table, as exported. Nothing on this page is typed in.

